A misspelled parameter (sRegoin for sRegion) and a name that is a
parameter of another procedure are not parameters of this scope, so both
fire diag.default_on_declare_line, even directly after :PARAMETERS.
Names compare case-insensitively, so SREGION is fine.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE RegionTotal;
	:PARAMETERS sRegion;
	:DEFAULT sRegoin, "north";
	:DEFAULT SREGION, "north";
	:DEFAULT nYear, 2024;
	:RETURN sRegion;
:ENDPROC;
:PROCEDURE YearTotal;
	:PARAMETERS nYear;
	:DEFAULT nYear, 2024;
	:RETURN nYear;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE RegionTotal;
	:PARAMETERS sRegion;
	:DEFAULT sRegoin, "north";
	:DEFAULT SREGION, "north";
	:DEFAULT nYear, 2024;

	:RETURN sRegion;
:ENDPROC;

:PROCEDURE YearTotal;
	:PARAMETERS nYear;
	:DEFAULT nYear, 2024;

	:RETURN nYear;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:11-3:18 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'sRegoin' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
5:11-5:16 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'nYear' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
3:11-3:18 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'sRegoin' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
3:11-3:18 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'sRegoin' is not declared
5:11-5:16 error default_on_declare_line: ':DEFAULT' target 'nYear' is not a ':PARAMETERS' name here - ':DEFAULT' only supplies a fallback for a parameter; give a ':DECLARE'd variable its value with an assignment
